-- =====================================================================================================================
-- 010_foreign_key_indexes.sql
-- Covering indexes for foreign keys that no other index already serves. PostgreSQL does not index the referencing side of a foreign
-- key automatically; without these, deleting or updating a parent row (and RESTRICT / CASCADE checks) scans the whole child table.
-- Foreign keys that point at public.profiles (created_by, updated_by, ...) are deliberately NOT indexed: profiles are deactivated,
-- never deleted, so those checks never run in practice and the indexes would only slow writes.
-- The list was produced from pg_constraint / pg_index after migrations 001-009 (tests/schema_validation.sql fails if a new
-- foreign key is added without a covering index).
-- =====================================================================================================================
